<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Business</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Business</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-bus</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:02Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-bus" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1431?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-bus" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Airline Norse Atlantic files for bankruptcy, succumbing to aviation fuel costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3f6c63911b372e039065f3cb97e4e19fd025601592700757e30a0721b70ca6a</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airline-norse-atlantic-files-for-bankruptcy-succumbing-to-aviation-fuel-costs/a-80076728--deb84ffc1870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airline-norse-atlantic-files-for-bankruptcy-succumbing-to-aviation-fuel-costs/a-80076728?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The low-cost airline was only founded a few years ago and had been struggling to turn a profit. The spike in aviation fuel prices caused by the war in Iran has now driven Norway's Norse Atlantic into bankruptcy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Indian workers fill Germany's labor gaps but face hurdles and risks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23488867c96cb2818be559491e9fee29dee1a106e436408cc98bafd3ddcb8165</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indian-workers-fill-germany-s-labor-gaps-but-face-hurdles-and-risks/a-80072882--78ecce9504e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indian-workers-fill-germany-s-labor-gaps-but-face-hurdles-and-risks/a-80072882?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The number of Indians working in Germany has grown rapidly in recent years. But many continue to face challenges in the labor market. Some also fall victim to recruitment scams, leaving them vulnerable to exploitation.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>EU-Indonesia trade deal opens new markets, but challenges remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0b826aff572552bc6d27287721731c5d9c5525edf3e16aeff49af85a3a0ff76</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T13:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-indonesia-trade-deal-opens-new-markets-but-challenges-remain/a-80059568--6d93bfcf9a92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-indonesia-trade-deal-opens-new-markets-but-challenges-remain/a-80059568?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The agreement offers new export and investment opportunities for Jakarta and Brussels. But can Indonesia turn Europe's growing interest in its markets and critical minerals into sustainable gains at home?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German firms eye Africa as global trade shocks hit traditional markets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c22990c0319cb96106a68dd32367c89f60908238b129a53a34f8d453264f160</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T14:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-firms-eye-africa-as-global-trade-shocks-hit-traditional-markets/a-80047671--b64160bb0ab9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-firms-eye-africa-as-global-trade-shocks-hit-traditional-markets/a-80047671?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German businesses are optimistic about Africa, but Berlin's cautious approach to risk is holding them back from cashing in on the opportunities that their competitors from countries like the UAE and Turkey are seizing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>German auto workers on back foot as costs, competition bite</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d954712de92b6e10b9b28c4023542ccb502b9c74cd8e26b9c73b5432aee64b5b</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T08:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-auto-workers-on-back-foot-as-costs-competition-bite/a-80036111--50a0a19d14b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-auto-workers-on-back-foot-as-costs-competition-bite/a-80036111?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German auto workers profited during the industry's boom years, but are now increasingly being asked to trade past gains for future job security.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>How cautious investors are struggling to avoid the AI bubble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e06299c6aebf16db05f6190bfd2e5da0a5d4586f515e83304e3dc4e5d8967eff</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-cautious-investors-are-struggling-to-avoid-the-ai-bubble/a-80016412--863307befc9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-cautious-investors-are-struggling-to-avoid-the-ai-bubble/a-80016412?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Nvidia to Coreweave, AI and tech stocks have swung sharply in recent months. Some investors still see plenty of room to run, while others are trying to diversify — and finding it harder than expected.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia reinstates former CEO Jensen Huang despite China espionage scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5de9af46a1a1fe0895206f3156ffed3855c922adf2af53c68a52d8ccac81212</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926--88659c21678b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's board voted unanimously to bring back the disgraced CEO, who resigned this month amid news of his affairs. He's suspected of having had a relationship with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'I've lost her forever' — Why German voice actors are refusing to sign Netflix's AI contract</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8b29e578311ba4d9399667e9c683913b6e2f79058d3eef0d95778549d1429cc</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381--da3277b6e37b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For decades, Germans have known Hollywood's biggest stars through the same familiar voices. Now an AI clause in Netflix contracts is splitting the industry over whether it protects performers or exposes them.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Early Start Pension: Can child investment accounts help?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f4397cfc6ff26114d77407f018346d6624c838e752808f4071305ffb6d21baf</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-early-start-pension-can-child-investment-accounts-help/a-79852185--25ffc2424261.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-early-start-pension-can-child-investment-accounts-help/a-79852185?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany plans to pay €10 a month into investment accounts for children to encourage long-term retirement saving. Economists say the measure may help build wealth but won't solve the country's pension funding challenge.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Lufthansa to cut 1,000 jobs, citing ongoing losses — reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:701e1877b412f0d07cb847452f036915754cb21300b232230c17166a6caa9e84</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T09:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062--a7b4260396ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">According to a letter obtained by the media, Lufthansa's executive board said the German company is losing €20 million every month. In addition to job cuts, operational cuts are also planned.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Anthropic trading tests investors' appetite for AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8305ddc9c833179645480c5495ec4c48a09445c3391c4a6fd4050f52b245a881</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/anthropic-trading-tests-investors-appetite-for-ai/a-79993163--d18c2700770b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/anthropic-trading-tests-investors-appetite-for-ai/a-79993163?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anthropic was valued at $2 trillion after shares started trading on the Nasdaq following a record $81 billion IPO. Its performance will put investor confidence in AI to the test.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Iran balances ties with China and Russia as Trump ramps up pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d3fa94583c62ff14299e7fef535be0205f48cdff80e6097a053a4be7f2e9ad7</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-balances-ties-with-china-and-russia-as-trump-ramps-up-pressure/a-79979920--3c92417b16df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-balances-ties-with-china-and-russia-as-trump-ramps-up-pressure/a-79979920?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Donald Trump seeks to tighten economic pressure on Iran, China remains its biggest oil customer and Russia a key partner. But both powers are balancing support for Tehran against broader interests with Washington.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Is the AI bubble bursting just as Anthropic goes public?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dd75e4a463463c1d9151b335884222ca10a8ebf6c66c4cb5e6d14764420dbea</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537--10f78cdc2264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sharp sell-off in tech stocks after the US midterms and the Nvidia scandal has cast doubt on Anthropic's IPO. Yet with hundreds of billions still being invested, some think the AI party is still in full swing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia forms national security committee after Huang affair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac9e9db9edbca8ae0350b9b8675a823ffce8440aa0c1478674509b861f63c12f</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T14:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-forms-national-security-committee-after-huang-affair/a-79970447--7d1c93df3ff0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-forms-national-security-committee-after-huang-affair/a-79970447?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia has created a board-level committee for national security and export control. This follows the resignation of CEO Jensen Huang over extramarital affairs, allegedly including one with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Could the Airbus €3 billion loan row reignite a US-EU trade dispute?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e96c20e4708b64ef744a6dfe5775ad4f061a3f33a42ceb60a4970ef01fa8f04e</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-the-airbus-_3-billion-loan-row-reignite-a-us-eu-trade-dispute/a-79943075--30f362f3b820.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-the-airbus-€3-billion-loan-row-reignite-a-us-eu-trade-dispute/a-79943075?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US says a record €3 billion financing package for Airbus may conflict with a transatlantic aircraft-subsidy truce. EU officials insist the funding complies with market-based rules.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: Spy row, affairs leave Nvidia without its rockstar CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c2a689b6ad7506cd63c4be432ec0ad5fbd00e7b6e9c3cd7e25daad7e5d7d927</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972--e6a7da621d57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang, who built Nvidia into the world’s dominant AI chipmaker, is stepping down as CEO over extramarital affairs. DW examines how losing its figurehead will affect the firm and the US-China AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f92f4554ac703dae27150bf2bc3b4cc22ac4d8f2f25dd66fba3c71a17d59abeb</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Megaspeed and the battle to go high-end Nvidia chips into China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d538106e1eba50806ef72fd6b99c0cbc2d33dc7450569884208dc253525fffc8</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129--5e400fbb45fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy has shone a light on Megaspeed, the company she worked for. It is under investigation in the US for smuggling Nvidia chips into China, which it denies.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why Nvidia CEO's affair with alleged Chinese spy matters for AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2eefd5cff86fd9d9f87c8bc56530d6ee9eace603113f236383a4bf9f7375653b</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-nvidia-ceo-s-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy-matters-for-ai-race/a-79898338--07d9155781b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-nvidia-ceo-s-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy-matters-for-ai-race/a-79898338?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang has apologized for an affair with a woman the US believes was spying for China. The story could have profound implications for the world's most valuable company and the global AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Amid protests, France's rising debt costs threaten stability</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3d16d78e606668e77de7aaa305e9997b11044c8611675b4c4c5b987a31d95e7</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654--50648477f294.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France plans to spend an extra €4 billion on education amid nationwide protests. But with public debt mounting and interest costs climbing, how much fiscal room does the government have?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry></feed>
